{"experiments":[  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Patients with higher tumor mutation burden (TMB) exhibit increased expression of immune checkpoint genes CD274 (PD-L1) and CTLA4.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Quantify TMB per patient and assess its correlation with CD274 and CTLA4 expression levels.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and cleaned_gene_expression.csv.  2. In mutation data, count total mutations per bcr_patient_barcode to define TMB.  3. Load expression data, strip Ensembl version suffixes, and extract CD274 (ENSG00000120217) and CTLA4 (ENSG00000163599) expression values.  4. Merge TMB and gene expression per patient.  5. Compute Spearman correlation between TMB and each gene’s expression.  6. Define TMB tertiles (Low, Mid, High) and compare CD274 and CTLA4 expression across tertiles using Kruskal-Wallis test.  7. Generate scatter plots of TMB vs expression with a fitted smoothing line and boxplots of expression by TMB tertile.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Table of TMB distribution.  2. Spearman rho and p-values for TMB vs CD274 and CTLA4.  3. Kruskal-Wallis test statistics and post-hoc pairwise p-values.  4. Scatter plots and boxplots illustrating the relationships."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Tumors harboring TP53 mutations display higher proliferation signature scores compared to TP53 wildtype tumors.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test whether TP53-mutant patients have elevated expression of proliferation markers.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and cleaned_gene_expression.csv.  2. Identify patients with at least one TP53 mutation (Hugo_Symbol='TP53').  3. Strip Ensembl versions in expression data and extract MKI67 (ENSG00000148773), PCNA (ENSG00000108342), CCNB1 (ENSG00000134057), BIRC5 (ENSG00000089685).  4. For each patient, compute a proliferation signature score as the mean expression of these four genes.  5. Label patients as TP53-mutant or TP53-wildtype.  6. Compare signature scores between groups using Mann–Whitney U test.  7. Plot boxplots of proliferation scores by TP53 status.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Counts of TP53-mutant and wildtype patients.  2. Summary statistics (mean/median/IQR) of proliferation scores per group.  3. Mann–Whitney U statistic and p-value.  4. Boxplot visualizing group differences."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"HER2-positive breast tumors (IHC 3+ or FISH-positive) have a higher prevalence of activating PIK3CA mutations than HER2-negative tumors.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Evaluate the association between HER2 status and PIK3CA mutation frequency.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and cleaned_mutations.csv.  2. Define HER2-positive patients where her2_ihc_score='3+' or her2_fish_status='Positive'; define HER2-negative where her2_ihc_score in {'0','1+','2+'} and her2_fish_status!='Positive'.  3. Filter mutation data for Hugo_Symbol='PIK3CA' and count patients with ≥1 PIK3CA mutation.  4. Construct a 2×2 table: HER2 status × PIK3CA mutation presence.  5. Perform Fisher’s exact test.  6. Report odds ratio and p-value.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Contingency table of HER2 status vs PIK3CA mutation.  2. Fisher’s exact test results (odds ratio, 95% CI, p-value).  3. Bar chart of PIK3CA mutation rates by HER2 group."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Black or African American patients have lower expression of CD8A and GZMB—markers of cytotoxic T lymphocyte infiltration—compared to White patients.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Compare immune infiltration signatures between Black and White racial groups.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and cleaned_gene_expression.csv.  2. Subset clinical data to patients with race labelled 'BLACK OR AFRICAN AMERICAN' or 'WHITE'.  3. Strip version suffixes in expression data and extract CD8A (ENSG00000153563) and GZMB (ENSG00000100440).  4. Merge expression values with racial group per patient.  5. Compare gene expression between race groups using Mann–Whitney U test for each gene.  6. Adjust p-values for multiple testing (e.g., Benjamini-Hochberg).  7. Generate boxplots for CD8A and GZMB by race.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Sample sizes per race group.  2. Summary statistics of CD8A and GZMB expression by group.  3. Mann–Whitney U test statistics, raw and adjusted p-values.  4. Boxplots comparing expression levels."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Postmenopausal patients exhibit higher PIK3CA expression and lower apoptosis signature compared to premenopausal patients.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Assess differences in oncogenic and apoptotic gene expression by menopause status.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and cleaned_gene_expression.csv.  2. Define menopause groups: 'Pre' (menopause_status contains 'Pre') vs 'Post' (contains 'Post').  3. Strip Ensembl versions and extract PIK3CA (ENSG00000121879), BAX (ENSG00000087088), CASP3 (ENSG00000164305).  4. Compute an apoptosis signature score as the mean of BAX and CASP3 per patient.  5. Merge PIK3CA expression and apoptosis signature with menopause group.  6. Compare PIK3CA expression and apoptosis signature between groups via Mann–Whitney U tests.  7. Plot boxplots of both metrics by menopause status.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Counts of pre- and postmenopausal patients.  2. Summary (mean/median/IQR) of PIK3CA expression and apoptosis score by group.  3. Mann–Whitney U statistics and p-values.  4. Boxplots illustrating group comparisons."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Triple-negative breast cancer (ER-, PR-, HER2-) patients have a higher tumor mutation burden than hormone receptor-positive patients.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Compare TMB between triple-negative and hormone receptor-positive subtypes.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and cleaned_mutations.csv.  2. Define triple-negative: er_status='Negative' AND pr_status='Negative' AND her2_ihc_status='Negative'; define HR-positive: er_status='Positive' OR pr_status='Positive'.  3. Count total mutations per patient to calculate TMB.  4. Merge TMB with subtype labels.  5. Compare TMB distributions using Mann–Whitney U test.  6. Plot boxplots of TMB by subtype.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Sample sizes per subtype.  2. Summary statistics of TMB by group.  3. Mann–Whitney U statistic and p-value.  4. Boxplot comparing TMB between subtypes."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Higher pathologic stage (III/IV) is associated with up-regulation of angiogenesis-related genes VEGFA, ANGPT2, and PGF compared to stage I/II tumors.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test whether advanced-stage tumors have elevated angiogenesis gene expression.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and cleaned_gene_expression.csv.  2. Define stage groups: early (pathologic_stage contains 'I' or 'II') vs advanced (contains 'III' or 'IV').  3. Strip version suffixes; extract VEGFA (ENSG00000112715), ANGPT2 (ENSG00000164254), PGF (ENSG00000124428).  4. Compute an angiogenesis signature score as the mean expression of these three genes.  5. Merge signature scores with stage group.  6. Compare scores using Mann–Whitney U test.  7. Generate boxplot of signature by stage.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Counts of early vs advanced stage patients.  2. Summary (mean/median/IQR) of angiogenesis scores by group.  3. Mann–Whitney U statistic and p-value.  4. Boxplot showing angiogenesis signature differences."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"PIK3CA-mutated tumors exhibit higher PIK3CA mRNA expression compared to PIK3CA-wildtype tumors.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Determine if activating PIK3CA mutations correlate with increased gene expression.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv and cleaned_gene_expression.csv.  2. Identify patients carrying ≥1 PIK3CA mutation (Hugo_Symbol='PIK3CA').  3. Strip Ensembl versions; extract PIK3CA expression (ENSG00000121879).  4. Merge expression with PIK3CA mutation status per patient.  5. Compare PIK3CA expression between mutant and wildtype groups using Mann–Whitney U test.  6. Plot boxplot of PIK3CA expression by mutation status.",  
      "deliverables":"1. Number of PIK3CA-mutant and wildtype patients.  2. Summary statistics (mean/median/IQR) of PIK3CA expression per group.  3. Mann–Whitney U statistic and p-value.  4. Boxplot of expression differences."  
    }  
  }  
]}
